#: ../../source/index.rst:12
msgid ""
"biwipy is a Python library that allows you to study the impact of wind on"
" cycling routes described by GPS tracks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:16
msgid ""
"Packaging transition (Phase 1): the published distribution name is "
"``biwipy`` while the Python import namespace remains ``refwindcycle`` for"
" backward compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:20
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:26
msgid "It provides:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:28
msgid ""
"retrospective analysis of actual routes already traveled (replay) in "
"order to observe the impact of wind after the fact and measure the effort"
" expended (power calculation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:30
msgid "simulation of planned routes up to the current date plus 16 days"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:32
msgid ""
"The biwipy library is based on a model of the physical laws of cycling , "
"incorporating continuous wind calculations using weather forecast data "
"files (GRIB files)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:34
msgid "Among the most interesting features of this model are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:36
msgid "the physical model of cycling performance is highly configurable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:38
msgid ""
"the model introduces  the concept of virtual elevation gain (positive and"
" negative)  which represents the equivalent “elevation gain” of wind "
"effects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:40
msgid ""
"The result of a simulation is summarized by a “windscore,” a grade "
"between A and F that incorporates safety and performance aspects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:42
msgid ""
"The library incorporates all the functions required for managing and "
"downloading GRIB files, pre-processing GPX files, and analysing the "
"simulation results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:45
msgid ""
"The library also comes with a set of sample programs that allow you to "
"quickly perform simulations and analyze cycling routes in a real-world "
"context with wind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:47
msgid ""
"This tool is designed to be as general as possible and usable by all "
"types of cyclists exposed to wind conditions, regardless of their level "
"or cycling practices (competition, leisure, cycle touring)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:49
msgid "Some concrete examples of questions that biwipy can help you answer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:51
msgid ""
"For my usual ride next week, which day is the most favorable, and which "
"days should I avoid ?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:53
msgid ""
"I would like to analyze the effort and wind conditions of my previous "
"rides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:55
msgid ""
"I want to go out tomorrow, but the wind forecast is not favorable. Among "
"the routes I am considering, I would like to identify the most favorable "
"and least dangerous one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:57
msgid ""
"I have a multi-stage bike trip planned for the next few days. What is the"
" best day to leave for the best wind conditions ?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/index.rst:59
msgid ""
"Professional runners sometimes seem to run in hellish winds. I would love"
" to measure these conditions.  ?"
msgstr ""

